<TUV xml:lang='zh-HANS' uptodate='0'></TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US' struct='1'><PARA><FC fs='180'>This is the requestSeed level used for ECU programming.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA><FC fs='180'>The Security Access Data Record is optional (consider using the newer 0x29 service).</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC fs='180'>CANdesc supports it as a callout to the application.</FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC fs='180'>DCM supports it. </FC>
</PARA>
<PARA list='bul'><FC fs='180'>Data-driven testers do not support it out of the box.</FC>
</PARA>
</TUV>
<TUV xml:lang='zh-HANS' uptodate='0' struct='1'></TUV>
</DESC>
